01:23:00.100 --> 01:23:03.433
- I try not to ask my mom about my dad,


01:23:03.437 --> 01:23:07.271
not because I think that she
doesn't have any good memories.


01:23:07.274 --> 01:23:10.812
More because again I don't want


01:23:10.819 --> 01:23:15.734
to draw up any painful ones.


01:23:15.741 --> 01:23:17.481
It was terrible and tragic


01:23:17.493 --> 01:23:18.858
what she had to go through,


01:23:18.869 --> 01:23:22.862
so she had to do something
different with her life.


01:23:22.873 --> 01:23:24.784
She had to leave all that behind.


01:23:24.791 --> 01:23:26.156
Shortly after all of that,


01:23:26.168 --> 01:23:27.783
she had her show, AM LA.


01:23:27.794 --> 01:23:30.285
She defined who she was.


01:23:30.297 --> 01:23:31.377
She rebuilt her life,


01:23:31.381 --> 01:23:33.463
and she rebuilt it in a fantastic way.


01:23:34.343 --> 01:23:35.628
- And credit to her, I get it.


01:23:35.636 --> 01:23:36.546
I understand it,


01:23:36.553 --> 01:23:39.010
that you're trying to keep a roof


01:23:39.014 --> 01:23:43.974
and keep a normal, stable
household for your kids.


01:23:46.271 --> 01:23:47.101
Guess what?


01:23:47.105 --> 01:23:48.015
It's fucking gone.


01:23:50.108 --> 01:23:53.396
Stability and sanity
left the fucking house


01:23:53.403 --> 01:23:55.610
two years ago when he got arrested.


01:23:58.200 --> 01:24:00.942
- I had to do an art project for school,


01:24:00.953 --> 01:24:03.035
and we had to do appropriation,


01:24:03.038 --> 01:24:06.451
so I appropriated this painting.


01:24:06.458 --> 01:24:11.077
On this side, there's photographs
of everything perfect,


01:24:11.088 --> 01:24:13.420
and as it goes on,


01:24:13.423 --> 01:24:17.382
I started to put in the articles


01:24:17.386 --> 01:24:19.422
from this perfect life


01:24:19.429 --> 01:24:21.465
to this destroyed life,


01:24:21.473 --> 01:24:22.553
and on the bumper, it says,


01:24:22.558 --> 01:24:25.220
"Destroy my childhood," for DMC.


01:24:30.607 --> 01:24:32.063
-  All right, man, you good?


01:24:32.067 --> 01:24:33.227
-  Yes--


01:24:33.235 --> 01:24:34.520
-  We get any last looks on Alec?


01:24:34.528 --> 01:24:35.358
-  I got some--


01:24:35.362 --> 01:24:36.192
-  We're good.


01:24:36.196 --> 01:24:37.026
We're ready to go.


01:24:37.030 --> 01:24:37.860
-  That's fine.


01:24:37.864 --> 01:24:38.694
Let's go.


01:24:38.699 --> 01:24:39.529
Let's shoot it.


01:24:39.533 --> 01:24:43.867
- I'd love to figure out,
what's the actual turning point?


01:24:43.870 --> 01:24:45.610
When does DeLorean get to a point


01:24:45.622 --> 01:24:47.112
where he could have turned back


01:24:48.333 --> 01:24:50.870
and maybe avoided everything?


01:24:50.877 --> 01:24:54.665
And whether he went on to
complete the car project or not,


01:24:54.673 --> 01:24:57.210
he would have lived to
fight another battle


01:24:57.217 --> 01:25:00.880
or try another iteration of all that


01:25:00.887 --> 01:25:01.876
and probably succeeded


01:25:01.888 --> 01:25:03.549
'cause he's a very clever guy.


01:25:03.557 --> 01:25:07.641
What's that moment where you
sit there and go too late?


01:25:07.644 --> 01:25:09.100
Is it the cocaine deal itself?


01:25:09.104 --> 01:25:11.311
Is it before that?


01:25:11.315 --> 01:25:12.805
Is it a series of things?


01:25:12.816 --> 01:25:16.058
Is it a period of time where
he's doing a few things?


01:25:16.069 --> 01:25:19.812
When does John put in all
the chips on the table,


01:25:19.823 --> 01:25:21.529
and he loses?


01:25:28.165 --> 01:25:31.157
- I saw the drug trial as a sideshow.


01:25:31.168 --> 01:25:35.707
To me, much more
substantial was how DeLorean


01:25:35.714 --> 01:25:37.454
was handling the money


01:25:37.466 --> 01:25:38.672
that he had gotten to build


01:25:38.675 --> 01:25:40.586
the car in Northern Ireland.


01:25:42.721 --> 01:25:45.007
- Every piece of paper tells a story


01:25:45.015 --> 01:25:46.095
of what people were doing


01:25:46.099 --> 01:25:47.259
and how they were doing it.


01:25:47.267 --> 01:25:48.757
Well, this transaction happened


01:25:48.769 --> 01:25:50.259
before this transaction,


01:25:50.270 --> 01:25:52.101
and that led to this transaction.


01:25:52.105 --> 01:25:54.721
I was brought in to analyze the affairs


01:25:54.733 --> 01:25:55.643
of DeLorean Motor Company


01:25:55.651 --> 01:25:57.812
and go deep into its affairs


01:25:57.819 --> 01:26:00.481
its activities and its transactions.


01:26:00.489 --> 01:26:01.945
We didn't really understand that at first,


01:26:01.948 --> 01:26:04.030
but it turned out to
be the critical moment


01:26:04.034 --> 01:26:07.117
in untangling the
affairs of John DeLorean,


01:26:07.120 --> 01:26:08.576
and as it became clear,


01:26:08.580 --> 01:26:11.947
you start to see yet again
another side of John.


01:26:13.168 --> 01:26:14.704
When the company was developing


01:26:14.711 --> 01:26:17.202
in those heady days of
excitement and energy


01:26:17.214 --> 01:26:18.545
around the company, around John,


01:26:18.548 --> 01:26:20.664
investors all wanted to get a piece of it.


01:26:21.718 --> 01:26:23.299
-  In trying to
raise all the capital,


01:26:23.303 --> 01:26:25.419
John was really selling himself.


01:26:25.430 --> 01:26:27.591
He was selling his image.


01:26:27.599 --> 01:26:29.055
The slogan, "Live the Dream,"


01:26:29.059 --> 01:26:31.391
that's what people were
supposedly buying into


01:26:31.395 --> 01:26:33.010
when they invested in his company.


01:26:33.021 --> 01:26:34.852
- And John, sensing that interest


01:26:34.856 --> 01:26:36.892
and wanting to raise
money if it was available,


01:26:36.900 --> 01:26:39.437
was able to raise $17 and a half million


01:26:39.444 --> 01:26:42.231
for the development of the vehicle,


01:26:42.239 --> 01:26:43.319
but as it turns out,


01:26:43.323 --> 01:26:46.440
the British government had also
put up enough money by then


01:26:46.451 --> 01:26:48.362
that their funds were actually being used


01:26:48.370 --> 01:26:50.452
to pay for the development of the vehicle,


01:26:50.455 --> 01:26:52.116
and therefore this money wasn't needed


01:26:52.124 --> 01:26:53.864
so much at that point,


01:26:53.875 --> 01:26:57.538
and John, seeing this pot
of money, couldn't resist.


01:26:57.546 --> 01:26:59.628
-  Federal investigators
and bankruptcy lawyers


01:26:59.631 --> 01:27:03.089
say they have uncovered
another secret DeLorean deal,


01:27:03.093 --> 01:27:06.381
this one arranged at a hotel
in Geneva, Switzerland,


01:27:06.388 --> 01:27:08.219
long before the alleged drug deal.


01:27:09.266 --> 01:27:12.884
-  A deal had been
struck in Switzerland


01:27:12.894 --> 01:27:14.009
with Colin Chapman,


01:27:14.020 --> 01:27:15.976
the chairman of Lotus,


01:27:15.981 --> 01:27:20.566
and the mysterious organization
called GPD Services.


01:27:21.528 --> 01:27:24.065
-  And what's
interesting becomes very clear


01:27:24.072 --> 01:27:27.360
that Bill Collins was onto
something several years earlier


01:27:27.367 --> 01:27:30.700
when he was analyzing the
DeLorean, Lotus agreement.


01:27:30.704 --> 01:27:31.944
- When I looked at the numbers


01:27:31.955 --> 01:27:32.944
that they put together,


01:27:32.956 --> 01:27:34.162
I said to John,


01:27:34.166 --> 01:27:35.576
"What's the deal?"


01:27:35.584 --> 01:27:37.199
GPD?


01:27:37.210 --> 01:27:38.199
I've never even heard of it.


01:27:38.211 --> 01:27:39.747
It just seems like you're paying twice


01:27:39.755 --> 01:27:41.165
for the same thing, John.


01:27:41.173 --> 01:27:43.004
Obviously looking back on it now,


01:27:43.008 --> 01:27:44.919
there were things going
on behind the scene.


01:27:44.926 --> 01:27:48.134
John and Chapman were trying to figure out


01:27:48.138 --> 01:27:50.754
the game they were playing with GPD


01:27:50.766 --> 01:27:55.681
and trying to get various
arrangements put together.


01:27:56.188 --> 01:27:57.769
- In the scene we shot yesterday,


01:27:57.773 --> 01:27:59.764
he hangs up with Collins,


01:27:59.775 --> 01:28:02.733
and everybody who's good,


01:28:02.736 --> 01:28:04.522
they've all got to go, you know?


01:28:04.529 --> 01:28:06.861
Because their goodness
becomes useless to John.


01:28:07.908 --> 01:28:10.115
They just don't do me any good.


01:28:10.118 --> 01:28:13.076
- Apart from denying that
he had any of the GPD money,


01:28:13.079 --> 01:28:16.116
John DeLorean is reluctant to discuss GPD.


01:28:16.124 --> 01:28:18.615
-  Can you give that an
answer now to those allegations


01:28:18.627 --> 01:28:20.868
about the missing $17 million?


01:28:25.133 --> 01:28:28.170
- So now we fast forward
into the investigation,


01:28:28.178 --> 01:28:31.295
and we start peeling
back the layers of GPD.


01:28:31.306 --> 01:28:36.266
- GPD is supposedly this middleman company


01:28:36.436 --> 01:28:41.100
to deliver certain other
engineering services.


01:28:41.107 --> 01:28:45.942
In truth, it had no other engineers.


01:28:45.946 --> 01:28:48.153
It had no facilities


01:28:48.156 --> 01:28:50.863
to deliver these engineering services.


01:28:50.867 --> 01:28:54.030
GPD was a mailbox.


01:28:54.037 --> 01:28:56.779
-  GPD is a phony, a shell company,


01:28:56.790 --> 01:28:59.623
nothing more than a post office
box in a neighborhood branch


01:28:59.626 --> 01:29:01.207
of the Geneva Post Office,


01:29:01.211 --> 01:29:02.917
Post Office Box 33.


01:29:04.589 --> 01:29:06.830
-  It turns out John made a deal


01:29:06.842 --> 01:29:09.254
with Colin Chapman at Lotus Cars


01:29:09.261 --> 01:29:11.673
that he would send the
$17 and a half million


01:29:11.680 --> 01:29:14.137
from investors into GPD,


01:29:14.140 --> 01:29:16.222
and then Colin took the money from there,


01:29:16.226 --> 01:29:18.592
funneled it into European bank accounts,


01:29:18.603 --> 01:29:20.184
split it with John.


01:29:20.188 --> 01:29:21.849
John then maneuvered that money


01:29:21.857 --> 01:29:24.599
back to his own accounts
in the United States,


01:29:24.609 --> 01:29:26.691
therefore converting the investor money


01:29:26.695 --> 01:29:27.901
into his own money.


01:29:32.367 --> 01:29:35.325
- I think there's a real
fascinating allegory here.


01:29:35.328 --> 01:29:37.944
You did sell your soul, John DeLorean.


01:29:37.956 --> 01:29:41.073
You sold it for the greater
glory of John DeLorean


01:29:41.084 --> 01:29:42.699
who was going to whip General Motors


01:29:42.711 --> 01:29:44.076
and all these multibillion dollar,


01:29:44.087 --> 01:29:46.669
multinational companies
with your own dream car,


01:29:46.673 --> 01:29:48.288
and in that vision,


01:29:48.300 --> 01:29:51.292
not only did you jeopardize
the well being of your family,


01:29:51.303 --> 01:29:53.385
you've risked yourself for a jail term,


01:29:53.388 --> 01:29:55.299
got off because the government blew it.


01:29:55.307 --> 01:29:57.138
Now we have other indictments,


01:29:57.142 --> 01:30:00.134
which indicate that it's possible


01:30:00.145 --> 01:30:03.888
that your fatigue and your egomania


01:30:03.899 --> 01:30:06.231
forced you to use money
for your own purpose


01:30:06.234 --> 01:30:08.771
rather than the original
intent of the investors.


01:30:08.778 --> 01:30:11.861
That's what seems to be
most apparent to anybody


01:30:11.865 --> 01:30:13.150
who gives a cursory review


01:30:13.158 --> 01:30:14.694
of the evidence in this case.


01:30:14.701 --> 01:30:16.817
- Well, as I said early on,


01:30:16.828 --> 01:30:19.365
I think that we will prove conclusively


01:30:19.372 --> 01:30:21.738
that every single cent was legitimately


01:30:21.750 --> 01:30:24.082
and honestly come by,


01:30:24.085 --> 01:30:27.077
and that all these
charges are totally false.


01:30:29.716 --> 01:30:33.174
- So as these questions
are being brought up


01:30:33.178 --> 01:30:36.841
and John is preparing to have
to answer these questions,


01:30:36.848 --> 01:30:39.305
he needed to show some sort of proof


01:30:39.309 --> 01:30:41.891
that made the deal not look shady,


01:30:41.895 --> 01:30:44.307
and that proof was actually a loan letter


01:30:44.314 --> 01:30:45.804
from GPD Services


01:30:45.815 --> 01:30:48.932
and a paper trail that GPD services


01:30:48.944 --> 01:30:50.275
was a loan to him


01:30:50.278 --> 01:30:51.814
and that he still had several years


01:30:51.821 --> 01:30:54.312
before he had to pay back that loan.


01:30:54.324 --> 01:30:56.315
He puts together these documents


01:30:56.326 --> 01:30:59.739
that only he and one other
person would be privy to,


01:30:59.746 --> 01:31:01.987
and that being Colin Chapman from Lotus.


01:31:01.998 --> 01:31:03.613
Well, several years earlier,


01:31:03.625 --> 01:31:06.662
Colin Chapman dropped
dead of a heart attack,


01:31:06.670 --> 01:31:08.456
and the only other person


01:31:08.463 --> 01:31:12.422
in this little transaction was John.


01:31:12.425 --> 01:31:14.131
- So while I was busy studying the records


01:31:14.135 --> 01:31:16.126
and looking at financial transactions,


01:31:16.137 --> 01:31:19.379
the lawyers were busy
talking to Cristina Ferrare.


01:31:19.391 --> 01:31:22.633
Cristina testified under oath


01:31:22.644 --> 01:31:27.104
that she saw John
working in a large closet


01:31:27.107 --> 01:31:31.521
with latex gloves on, signing documents,


01:31:31.528 --> 01:31:34.520
backdating them, and
then aging the documents


01:31:34.531 --> 01:31:36.067
under a sun lamp


01:31:36.074 --> 01:31:37.029
so when the documents


01:31:37.033 --> 01:31:39.149
would be forensically examined later on,


01:31:39.160 --> 01:31:40.900
his fingerprints wouldn't be on it.


01:31:40.912 --> 01:31:42.573
His skin oil wouldn't be on it,


01:31:42.580 --> 01:31:43.615
and of course the paper would


01:31:43.623 --> 01:31:45.113
have aged under the sun lamp,


01:31:45.125 --> 01:31:47.332
and she testified that
she saw him do that,


01:31:47.335 --> 01:31:49.451
so John was very busy


01:31:49.462 --> 01:31:50.952
creating a set of documents


01:31:50.964 --> 01:31:52.295
in the dark of night,


01:31:52.298 --> 01:31:54.334
but his wife was watching him.


01:31:57.345 --> 01:31:59.131
After reviewing the records,


01:31:59.139 --> 01:32:01.596
there came a time when the trial started


01:32:01.599 --> 01:32:03.590
to recover this money that John had taken


01:32:03.601 --> 01:32:04.841
from the company,


01:32:04.853 --> 01:32:05.933
and I started to really get


01:32:05.937 --> 01:32:08.223
a good look at John as a person


01:32:08.231 --> 01:32:10.688
and the true nature of his character,


01:32:10.692 --> 01:32:12.273
so he walks in court one day,


01:32:12.277 --> 01:32:13.107
and then he looks at me,


01:32:13.111 --> 01:32:14.942
and he says, "I was on
the radio this morning.


01:32:14.946 --> 01:32:17.813
"I was talking about
you and your testimony."


01:32:17.824 --> 01:32:20.315
He goes, "But I'm not sure
I got your name right."


01:32:20.326 --> 01:32:22.988
He said, "Is there one
H in Shithead or two?"


01:32:24.497 --> 01:32:25.327
And I said, wow,


01:32:26.750 --> 01:32:29.867
but by then I also realized we had him.


01:32:29.878 --> 01:32:31.709
In other words, he was acting out


01:32:31.713 --> 01:32:33.078
because we knew we had him.


01:32:33.089 --> 01:32:35.421
Between us having the financial evidence


01:32:35.425 --> 01:32:37.882
and Cristina would testify


01:32:37.886 --> 01:32:41.595
that John had been forging
documents and aging documents,


01:32:41.598 --> 01:32:43.429
John needed to settle that case,


01:32:43.433 --> 01:32:45.139
actually cough up the money


01:32:45.143 --> 01:32:47.509
that had been stolen from the investors


01:32:47.520 --> 01:32:49.306
in the DeLorean partnership.


01:32:49.314 --> 01:32:50.975
-  Would you deny
therefore that you had


01:32:50.982 --> 01:32:52.768
any of that $17 million?


01:32:52.776 --> 01:32:53.936
- Excuse me a minute.


01:32:53.943 --> 01:32:55.729
I have to get a drink.


01:32:55.737 --> 01:32:57.193
-  John DeLorean was not prepared


01:32:57.197 --> 01:32:58.562
to answer any further questions


01:32:58.573 --> 01:33:00.780
about the missing $17.6 million.


01:33:08.541 --> 01:33:10.702
- In the drug trial, John
really could grasp on


01:33:10.710 --> 01:33:11.825
to that idea of,


01:33:11.836 --> 01:33:14.122
"I was the victim here.


01:33:14.130 --> 01:33:18.373
"I got sucked into a situation
of overzealous people,


01:33:18.384 --> 01:33:21.046
"overzealous government, that
was trying to take me down


01:33:21.054 --> 01:33:23.010
"as a legitimate business owner.


01:33:23.014 --> 01:33:25.676
In the case of the money trials,


01:33:25.683 --> 01:33:28.015
it's very hard to take the approach


01:33:28.019 --> 01:33:29.259
that he was the victim


01:33:29.270 --> 01:33:31.682
because all of it was his own doing.


01:33:31.689 --> 01:33:34.271
-  You start to see
this real true character,


01:33:34.275 --> 01:33:36.516
this underlying nature of John,


01:33:36.528 --> 01:33:38.985
not the public persona
that he had worked so hard


01:33:38.988 --> 01:33:40.694
to cultivate for years.


01:33:40.698 --> 01:33:44.737
- He had built this
giant bubble of an image


01:33:44.744 --> 01:33:46.234
making him believe he could


01:33:46.246 --> 01:33:47.861
kind of get away with anything.


01:33:48.832 --> 01:33:51.995
This was not the little guy fighting


01:33:52.001 --> 01:33:54.037
the Goliath like GM.


01:33:54.045 --> 01:33:57.503
This instead was someone
in his business dealings


01:33:57.507 --> 01:33:59.623
who acted like the Goliath


01:33:59.634 --> 01:34:02.842
and trampled on other people's dreams


01:34:02.846 --> 01:34:07.089
and really hurt some
individuals very badly.


01:34:07.100 --> 01:34:08.306
- I'm not a psychiatrist,


01:34:08.309 --> 01:34:12.143
but I think that he was
okay in the beginning,


01:34:12.147 --> 01:34:14.433
and I think he just got carried away.


01:34:15.316 --> 01:34:16.806
I think that he could have saved it


01:34:16.818 --> 01:34:18.649
if he'd had the right attitude,


01:34:18.653 --> 01:34:20.234
but I think he thought
it was more important


01:34:20.238 --> 01:34:23.981
to make a buck than to be successful.


01:34:25.285 --> 01:34:27.401
- That is part of the real tragedy


01:34:27.412 --> 01:34:29.528
in going back to the what ifs.


01:34:34.377 --> 01:34:37.119
and he had still had $17 and half million


01:34:37.130 --> 01:34:39.337
at the time when he
needed desperately cash


01:34:39.340 --> 01:34:40.500
to keep the company open?


01:34:40.508 --> 01:34:41.338
- We're the FBI.


01:34:41.342 --> 01:34:43.082
-  By stealing that money,


01:34:43.094 --> 01:34:45.426
John really painted himself into a corner,


01:34:45.430 --> 01:34:47.921
and he had to find the
money somewhere else,


01:34:47.932 --> 01:34:50.139
and to think if he could have only held on


01:34:50.143 --> 01:34:51.508
for a few more years.


01:35:06.159 --> 01:35:06.944
- Doc.


01:35:08.536 --> 01:35:10.151
- Marty, you made it.


01:35:10.163 --> 01:35:11.027
- Yeah.


01:35:11.039 --> 01:35:12.449
- Welcome to my latest experiment.


01:35:12.457 --> 01:35:13.287
This is the big one,


01:35:13.291 --> 01:35:15.452
the one I've been waiting for all my life.


01:35:15.460 --> 01:35:16.825
- Wow, it's a DeLorean, right--


01:35:16.836 --> 01:35:17.666
- Bear with me, Marty.


01:35:17.670 --> 01:35:18.625
All your questions will be answered.


01:35:18.630 --> 01:35:19.585
Roll tape--


01:35:19.589 --> 01:35:20.419
- Yeah, okay I'm rolling--


01:35:20.423 --> 01:35:22.835
- When Bob Zemeckis and I first
wrote "Back To The Future,‘'


01:35:22.842 --> 01:35:26.460
the time machine was a refrigerator,


01:35:26.471 --> 01:35:30.259
and Bob Zemeckis, the director, said,


01:35:30.266 --> 01:35:34.430
"Wouldn't it be simpler
if Doc actually built


01:35:34.437 --> 01:35:36.268
"the time machine into a car?"


01:35:36.272 --> 01:35:40.641
And then he says, "And what
if the car was a DeLorean?"


01:35:40.652 --> 01:35:41.607
It wasn't my idea


01:35:41.611 --> 01:35:43.522
but I know damn good idea when I hear one.


01:35:43.529 --> 01:35:45.315
This was a damn good idea,


01:35:45.323 --> 01:35:47.234
so I said, yeah, that's great.


01:35:47.242 --> 01:35:50.405
- When this baby hits 88 miles per hour,


01:35:50.411 --> 01:35:52.197
you're gonna see some serious shit.


01:35:57.460 --> 01:36:00.793
-  We, I think, did a great job


01:36:00.797 --> 01:36:03.004
in making the DeLorean glamorous


01:36:03.007 --> 01:36:06.124
and endearing it to generations


01:36:06.135 --> 01:36:09.548
of movie fans and car fans.


01:36:09.555 --> 01:36:11.967
- 88 miles per hour.


01:36:12.850 --> 01:36:15.432
- If only we'd stayed alive


01:36:15.436 --> 01:36:18.644
and we'd continued for another two years.


01:36:18.648 --> 01:36:21.560
You can't buy that publicity now, can you?


01:36:22.819 --> 01:36:25.811
-  "Back To The Futurell makes the car


01:36:25.822 --> 01:36:27.983
and the man truly immortal.


01:36:28.908 --> 01:36:30.773
100 years from now,


01:36:30.785 --> 01:36:32.241
people will watch that movie,


01:36:33.204 --> 01:36:35.490
and the last running DeLorean


01:36:35.498 --> 01:36:38.331
may have consumed its last drop of fuel


01:36:38.334 --> 01:36:40.040
and eaten its last piston,


01:36:40.044 --> 01:36:42.035
but that movie will carry on.


01:36:44.007 --> 01:36:45.167
- After the movie came out,


01:36:45.174 --> 01:36:47.039
about two or three weeks later,


01:36:47.051 --> 01:36:49.713
we got one of the best
fan letters we ever got,


01:36:49.721 --> 01:36:51.211
and it was from John DeLorean.


01:36:51.222 --> 01:36:54.009
He said that he'd just seen the movie.


01:36:54.017 --> 01:36:55.427
He thought it was brilliant,


01:36:56.686 --> 01:36:59.644
and he said, "Thank you for
keeping my dream alive."


01:37:03.609 --> 01:37:04.815
- Back in a time when


01:37:06.321 --> 01:37:10.815
I was lead to believe films
about him were percolating,


01:37:14.746 --> 01:37:15.576
there were a couple of them,


01:37:15.580 --> 01:37:16.535
to my recollection,


01:37:16.539 --> 01:37:17.904
that people were gonna make.


01:37:19.125 --> 01:37:20.205
I get a phone call,


01:37:22.545 --> 01:37:23.955
and it was DeLorean,


01:37:27.216 --> 01:37:29.002
and I have to imagine he was probably


01:37:30.303 --> 01:37:31.668
out of the house, the big house,


01:37:31.679 --> 01:37:32.964
and living in this apartment,


01:37:32.972 --> 01:37:35.839
the scene that we're gonna shoot today.


01:37:35.850 --> 01:37:36.930
Yeah, I was on the phone with him,


01:37:36.934 --> 01:37:42.019
and he was like, "Alex, this
is John DeLorean calling."


01:37:42.023 --> 01:37:42.853
He's very old.


01:37:42.857 --> 01:37:44.518
He sounded older.


01:37:44.525 --> 01:37:45.981
He said, "I understand they're making


01:37:45.985 --> 01:37:48.943
"this motion picture about me,


01:37:48.946 --> 01:37:52.780
"and I would be very flattered


01:37:52.784 --> 01:37:56.447
"if you were to portray me in the movie."


01:37:56.454 --> 01:37:59.241
I thought, wow,


01:37:59.248 --> 01:38:00.078
I mean, to have the guy


01:38:00.083 --> 01:38:01.038
who's the real guy pick you,


01:38:02.293 --> 01:38:04.784
and then it went away.


01:38:06.005 --> 01:38:08.121
I never heard from him again,


01:38:08.132 --> 01:38:10.714
but, I mean, to me,


01:38:10.718 --> 01:38:13.300
DeLorean is a lot of things.


01:38:13.304 --> 01:38:16.091
Every day, I think about who is he,


01:38:16.099 --> 01:38:18.135
I have a different answer.


01:38:18.142 --> 01:38:20.633
Today my attitude about DeLorean,


01:38:20.645 --> 01:38:22.931
you watch historical footage,


01:38:22.939 --> 01:38:25.681
and you get kind of inflamed


01:38:26.651 --> 01:38:28.357
of bad things to some people,


01:38:28.361 --> 01:38:29.771
and he hurt a lot of people,


01:38:29.779 --> 01:38:30.985
and he stole from people,


01:38:32.782 --> 01:38:33.771
and at the same time,


01:38:36.077 --> 01:38:38.159
I feel like he was somebody who,


01:38:39.080 --> 01:38:41.947
like a lot of great American stories,


01:38:41.958 --> 01:38:44.415
he just perverted some dream that he had.


01:38:47.630 --> 01:38:49.837
You remember the DMC, don't you?


01:38:49.841 --> 01:38:50.626
Yeah.


01:38:52.218 --> 01:38:53.799
How could you forget it, right?


01:38:53.803 --> 01:38:55.043
It was one of a kind.


01:38:56.973 --> 01:38:59.180
It really was one of a kind.


01:38:59.183 --> 01:39:02.971
- As full as John's life
was those first 60 years,


01:39:02.979 --> 01:39:06.597
the last 20 years are
actually more simple.


01:39:06.607 --> 01:39:09.019
This is one of John's Bibles


01:39:09.026 --> 01:39:12.860
which he actually gave to his nephew Mark.


01:39:12.864 --> 01:39:14.479
He became a born again Christian.


01:39:15.366 --> 01:39:17.527
It was a very important part of his life.


01:39:17.535 --> 01:39:19.571
He dated several women
throughout the years,


01:39:19.579 --> 01:39:21.615
and then ended up
re-marrying late in life,


01:39:21.622 --> 01:39:24.659
and then in 2000, had
to declare bankruptcy,


01:39:24.667 --> 01:39:27.158
in which he lost his Bedminster Estate


01:39:27.170 --> 01:39:29.206
and lived the last five years of his life


01:39:29.213 --> 01:39:30.623
in a one bedroom apartment.


01:39:31.674 --> 01:39:33.164
- His whole fucking life, his whole dream,


01:39:33.176 --> 01:39:35.292
everything that he worked for


01:39:35.303 --> 01:39:37.419
from the time they broke ground


01:39:37.430 --> 01:39:39.512
till the time of the arrest, gone.


01:39:44.228 --> 01:39:45.513
-  Was it a blow to your pride


01:39:45.521 --> 01:39:48.228
to you trying to shape your life again?


01:39:48.232 --> 01:39:51.349
- Well, I felt terrible
about it for a long time.


01:39:53.154 --> 01:39:55.395
who've this has been an extremely


01:39:55.406 --> 01:39:57.692
difficult thing for them,


01:39:57.700 --> 01:39:59.861
but life is life.


01:39:59.869 --> 01:40:00.733
It goes on.


01:40:02.038 --> 01:40:04.450
- Your father is shamed and goes to jail.


01:40:04.457 --> 01:40:06.038
Your family loses all their money.


01:40:06.042 --> 01:40:07.703
Your parents get divorced.


01:40:07.710 --> 01:40:09.416
Everything in your world changes,


01:40:09.420 --> 01:40:12.036
and for the next 15 years of your life


01:40:12.048 --> 01:40:14.835
you get chased by,


01:40:14.842 --> 01:40:16.173
"Is your father in jail?"


01:40:16.177 --> 01:40:17.542
And cocaine jokes,


01:40:17.553 --> 01:40:19.009
and all of these things


01:40:19.013 --> 01:40:21.095
that just followed along with it.


01:40:22.058 --> 01:40:25.471
My entire life I had to live it down.


01:40:26.771 --> 01:40:29.888
It followed me for a very long time.


01:40:29.899 --> 01:40:32.106
It followed me around until I started


01:40:32.109 --> 01:40:36.523
to get involved into
the DeLorean community.


01:40:38.658 --> 01:40:40.444
People used to invite my dad


01:40:40.451 --> 01:40:43.238
to all these car shows all the time,


01:40:43.246 --> 01:40:45.328
and I asked him.


01:40:45.331 --> 01:40:48.198
I said, Dad, Dad, let's go.


01:40:48.209 --> 01:40:50.416
You have to experience this.


01:40:50.419 --> 01:40:54.458
Knowing how much he was still loved


01:40:54.465 --> 01:40:57.252
would definitely make a
difference in his life.


01:40:59.178 --> 01:41:00.167
- Thank you.


01:41:01.347 --> 01:41:03.133
-  It was an amazing experience.


01:41:03.140 --> 01:41:05.677
It was everything I hoped it would be


01:41:05.685 --> 01:41:06.640
and then some.


01:41:06.644 --> 01:41:08.350
- I just met John DeLorean
for the third time.


01:41:08.354 --> 01:41:09.139
Document that.


01:41:10.189 --> 01:41:11.349
The man is unbelievable.


01:41:13.401 --> 01:41:16.359
-  He really did get to bask


01:41:16.362 --> 01:41:19.695
in his glory a little bit again.


01:41:23.536 --> 01:41:25.242
- Do you consider the whole DeLorean dream


01:41:25.246 --> 01:41:26.452
to have been a failure?


01:41:26.455 --> 01:41:28.411
- Oh, I think that I
showed a lot of people


01:41:28.416 --> 01:41:31.658
that whether you survive or not,


01:41:31.669 --> 01:41:33.500
the key is it's like Shakespeare said.


01:41:33.504 --> 01:41:34.914
"It's better to have loved and lost


01:41:34.922 --> 01:41:36.753
"than not to have loved at all."


01:41:36.757 --> 01:41:38.418
I gave it the best shot I had.


01:41:38.426 --> 01:41:40.291
I tried as hard as I could,


01:41:40.303 --> 01:41:44.467
and I think that I did reasonably well.


01:41:44.473 --> 01:41:45.303
It's a tragedy--


01:41:45.308 --> 01:41:48.095
- I think DeLorean was very much alone.


01:41:48.102 --> 01:41:51.435
Part of the fallout
from compartmentalizing


01:41:51.439 --> 01:41:53.395
his life the way he did


01:41:54.358 --> 01:41:58.317
is that he really didn't have anybody


01:41:58.321 --> 01:42:00.528
who knew him through and through.


01:42:01.657 --> 01:42:04.820
This is not a man who's
looking at his family life


01:42:04.827 --> 01:42:08.365
or his friends to qualify


01:42:08.372 --> 01:42:09.908
his reason for living.


01:42:09.915 --> 01:42:11.746
It's, "What have I accomplished?


01:42:11.751 --> 01:42:12.581
"What have I done?


01:42:12.585 --> 01:42:14.871
"What am I doing next?"


01:42:14.879 --> 01:42:16.119
That in his mind,


01:42:16.130 --> 01:42:19.122
this is what really reflects on him


01:42:19.133 --> 01:42:20.873
as a human being.


01:42:20.885 --> 01:42:21.795
- When we come around here,


01:42:21.802 --> 01:42:24.339
what I'd like to do is repeat this action


01:42:24.347 --> 01:42:25.883
and just put this down here


01:42:25.890 --> 01:42:27.175
and then look up at the car,


01:42:27.183 --> 01:42:28.263
and I want to say something very


01:42:28.267 --> 01:42:30.053
specific to him about the car.


01:42:30.061 --> 01:42:30.891
-  Cool.


01:42:30.895 --> 01:42:33.511
- No film can tell the definitive
story of anybody's life.


01:42:33.522 --> 01:42:36.229
Anyone's life is just too vast


01:42:36.233 --> 01:42:38.940
and complex for one film,


01:42:38.944 --> 01:42:42.186
but a film could certainly create


01:42:42.198 --> 01:42:43.984
the legend of John DeLorean,


01:42:43.991 --> 01:42:47.108
and we print the legend.


01:42:47.119 --> 01:42:48.859
The legend is what we love.


01:42:48.871 --> 01:42:50.702
That's what we should have.


01:42:53.584 --> 01:42:55.996
-  Let's just hypothetically say


01:42:56.003 --> 01:42:58.335
that when he went into
the hotel that night,


01:42:58.339 --> 01:42:59.795
he knew he was walking out


01:42:59.799 --> 01:43:01.710
with a suitcase full of cocaine.


01:43:02.677 --> 01:43:04.508
I can't necessarily blame him.


01:43:06.472 --> 01:43:08.713
How far would you be willing to go


01:43:08.724 --> 01:43:10.305
to save something you worked


01:43:10.309 --> 01:43:12.470
your whole life for, your life's dream?


01:43:12.478 --> 01:43:15.220
What would you do to see that succeed


01:43:15.231 --> 01:43:16.186
no matter what?


01:43:20.569 --> 01:43:22.434
- He always kept trying.


01:43:22.446 --> 01:43:25.313
He never gave up the dream.


01:43:25.324 --> 01:43:28.066
He never quit believing


01:43:28.077 --> 01:43:29.192
that there was a potential


01:43:29.203 --> 01:43:30.158
for him to recover,


01:43:30.162 --> 01:43:31.447
that he was going to invent


01:43:31.455 --> 01:43:32.410
the next great thing,


01:43:32.415 --> 01:43:33.655
that he was going to be able


01:43:33.666 --> 01:43:35.952
to reclaim his former glory.


01:43:35.960 --> 01:43:37.416
He was John DeLorean,


01:43:37.420 --> 01:43:40.833
and he was John DeLorean
until the day he died.


01:43:40.840 --> 01:43:41.670
- I think he was still


01:43:41.674 --> 01:43:44.837
trying to make fucking deals on that DMC-2


01:43:44.844 --> 01:43:46.380
when he got the heart attack,


01:43:48.139 --> 01:43:50.801
and I think that would be a
good way to end the movie.


01:43:51.934 --> 01:43:52.764
You could have him


01:43:52.768 --> 01:43:54.474
on the phone eating some breakfast


01:43:55.980 --> 01:43:58.187
with an open notebook thing


01:43:58.190 --> 01:43:59.430
that you'd show investors


01:43:59.442 --> 01:44:02.980
with all the nice little
pictures and stuff,


01:44:02.987 --> 01:44:04.022
talking on the phone,


01:44:04.029 --> 01:44:06.145
and then it just fades to black


01:44:06.157 --> 01:44:08.273
because then that last
image would just be him


01:44:08.284 --> 01:44:11.321
working to get that deal done,


01:44:11.328 --> 01:44:15.116
and God pulled the plug on his ass, man.


01:44:16.041 --> 01:44:17.281
You're out of here, buddy.


01:44:19.211 --> 01:44:20.917
Then it just goes black,


01:44:20.921 --> 01:44:22.331
and then John DeLorean died


01:44:22.339 --> 01:44:24.455
in Morristown, New Jersey,


01:44:24.467 --> 01:44:27.504
at fucking 80 years old
on this date, you know?


01:44:27.511 --> 01:44:31.129
Never to have fulfilled
another car company,


01:44:31.140 --> 01:44:33.096
build another car company,


01:44:33.100 --> 01:44:35.136
and I'd be okay with that.


01:44:35.144 --> 01:44:36.805
-  And slate, that's good.


01:44:37.646 --> 01:44:40.058
-  Scene 28 alpha, take two.


01:44:40.065 --> 01:44:42.101
-  Great, thank you.


01:44:46.071 --> 01:44:46.935
-  Action.


01:48:51.025 --> 01:48:51.855
- I mean, if we can't get the money


01:48:51.859 --> 01:48:53.440
to distribute this movie,


01:48:53.444 --> 01:48:54.604
would we sell cocaine to try


01:48:54.611 --> 01:48:55.726
to get this movie distributed?


01:48:55.738 --> 01:48:56.568
-  Sure.


01:48:56.572 --> 01:48:57.857
- We don't want to lose either.


01:48:57.865 --> 01:48:58.900
-  No.


01:48:58.907 --> 01:49:00.317
- I'm counting on you, Sheena.
